{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794157532,"nonce":"eEwFiezYLEMEEYgLdocamvhKZwY=","title":"The palette lists its own keys, and the bottom line is blank under it","message":"## Design\n\n**Aspect changed:** `doc/design/tui.md` (\"Keys on the palette\", \"The palette over a text\", \"Key hints are on the bottom line only\", \"Where you are\").\n\n- **Everything the palette answers is in the box.** Its letters already are; its other keys join them:\n  - `ctrl+c copy page command`, drawn dim at the end of the breadcrumb line, beside the call it copies;\n  - `esc back`, the last entry of *everywhere*, after `g close`;\n  - over a text, *this text* lists `e editor`, `g close`, `esc leave text`, and there is no `ctrl+c` beside the call, since it rings there.\n- **While the palette is open, the bottom line's hints are blank**; its right side keeps the last message.\n  - Not the page's line unchanged: its keys do not act while the palette is open, and its `? keys` repeats the box's `? help`.\n  - Not removing the line: a refusal or a *copied* would vanish until the palette closes.\n  - `paletteHints` and its `letter: run` go: a letter running is what a palette is.\n- **\"Key hints are on the bottom line only\"** gains the exception, with its reason: the palette is a menu, so its keys are its content. The search, flow picker and query editor are inputs, and keep their keys on the bottom line.\n\nDesign approved by Luis on 2026-11-08.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["tui"],"priority":"medium","status":"in-progress","type":"story"}}]}